					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1596175#post-3749818</guid>
				<title>Realized something when I finished the tales</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1596175/xiupania#post-3749818</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 26 Mar 2018 04:08:47 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Doctor GE Smith</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1786409</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I loved the imagery and ideas of this plot, but it just didn't feel right until I realized something while looking at the comments after finishing the most recent tale.<br /> A lot of people didn't like this because it <em>felt wrong</em> for the SCPverse. In a world of killer statues, Yellowstone disaster shelters, antimemes, and toilet ghosts, this felt too fanciful, a step too far.<br /> And that is what this is relative to the Foundation, who are &quot;happy&quot; to house all manner of almost-contained Keter objects. It is the step too far that they will burn humanity's dreams to expunge from the SCPverse.<br /> This subtle tone jump lets us see what the Foundation does when forced to confront their own blind spots. That's where a lot of my favorite SCPs and tales come from. +1 to all of the entries!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
